+//! Versioned protocol: two builds of this cluster, talking to each other for as long as it takes.
+//!
+//! `meshkv/5.21-protocol-evolution` is the last shape of the "two truths at once" problem this track
+//! has met three times: joint consensus (`5.5`) held two *memberships* at once, certificate rotation
+//! (`5.9`) held two *certificates*, and a rolling upgrade holds two **builds**.
+//!
+//! The rule is the same arithmetic in a different unit: during the upgrade, every node has to be able
+//! to understand every other node, or the cluster stops. Two numbers make that checkable:
+//!
+//! * the **major** version is the wire format. Two nodes with different majors cannot talk, so a
+//!   rolling upgrade may never have both in the cluster — which is what makes a major bump a
+//!   *stop-the-world* operation, stated rather than discovered;
+//! * the **minor** version is compatible within a major, and a node speaks every minor up to its own.
+//!   So a cluster may hold two minors during an upgrade, and the rule is that the *newer* peer must
+//!   not speak a minor the older one does not know.
+//!
+//! The upgrade is a plan, like `5.15`'s restart: an order over the nodes, and a check that every
+//! handshake along the way is possible. Upgrading every node at once is not a plan; upgrading one and
+//! then waiting is.
+//!
+//! The handshake carries the version for one reason: the moment a node sees a major it does not
+//! speak, the right answer is a refusal that names the version — not a frame that gets misread.
+
+use crate::cluster::NodeId;
+use crate::error::Result;
