+    /// An upgraded node speaks the *old* minor until the last node is upgraded — that is the hold-back
+    /// the asymmetry of [`Protocol::can_parse`] requires — and the last step is where the cluster
+    /// starts speaking the new one. The phases are what an operator reads off a deploy log.
+    ///
+    /// # Errors
+    ///
